---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Accordion from "../../components/ui/Accordion.astro";
import DataTable from "../../components/ui/DataTable.astro";
import FeatureSection from "../../components/ui/FeatureSection.astro";
import LinkList from "../../components/ui/LinkList.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/ui/PageHero.astro";
import StatGrid from "../../components/ui/StatGrid.astro";
import Timeline from "../../components/ui/Timeline.astro";
import VideoEmbed from "../../components/ui/VideoEmbed.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout locale="en" alternates={{ hu: "/bemutatkozas" }} title={"For more than 140 years, value has been the measure."} description={"The school opened on 7 December 1879 under the name State Industrial Secondary School – and since then it has been one of the oldest and most respected institutions of Hungarian vocational training."} canonicalPath={"/en/about-us"}>
  <PageHero breadcrumb={[{"label": "Home", "href": "/en"}, {"label": "About us"}]} title={"For more than 140 years, value has been the measure."} intro={"The school opened on 7 December 1879 under the name State Industrial Secondary School – and since then it has been one of the oldest and most respected institutions of Hungarian vocational training."} />
  <FeatureSection eyebrow={"The school's namesake"} title={"Petrik Lajos"} imageSide={"right"} html={"<p>The school's namesake, Lajos Petrik, was a teacher at the institution from 1880 and its director from 1905 to 1914. His career was characterised by openness to the challenges of science, the fine arts and nature. He was at once a scientist, teacher, ceramist, art collector and nature lover.</p>"} />
  <StatGrid items={[{"value": "1178", "label": "Student"}, {"value": "120", "label": "Teacher"}, {"value": "35", "label": "Classroom"}, {"value": "23", "label": "Laboratory"}]} columns={4} />
  <Timeline heading={"History of the school"} rows={[{"key": "1879", "text": "On 7 December the State Industrial Secondary School opens its doors, with mechanical engineering, architecture and chemistry specialisations. Its first building stood at 4 Főherceg Sándor (today Gutenberg) Square."}, {"key": "1889", "text": "The school moves into the new building complex designed by Alajos Hauszmann (at the corner of József körút and Népszínház utca). Its director is Károly Hegedűs, who led the institution for 35 years."}, {"key": "1898", "text": "Its new name is Royal Hungarian State Higher Industrial School; four main specialisations: mechanical engineering, chemical industry, metal and iron industry, woodworking industry."}, {"key": "1940", "text": "The chemical industry specialisation moves to the building at Thököly út 48, which is still the school's home today."}, {"key": "1990s", "text": "Alongside the traditional chemical industry training, IT and environmental protection training grows up. In 2007/2008, merging with the Irinyi János Secondary School of Environmental Protection and Chemical Industry, Petrik becomes the largest environmental protection and chemical industry training institution in the country."}, {"key": "2015", "text": "From 1 July the school's maintainer is the Budapest Technical Vocational Training Centre."}, {"key": "2019", "text": "The 140th anniversary of the founding of the school. In the HVG “Secondary School 2019” publication, it ranks 10th nationwide among vocational secondary schools."}]} />
  <Accordion heading={"About Our School"} items={[{"title": "Our creed and goals", "html": "<p>The versatility represented by our namesake, <strong>Lajos Petrik</strong>, and the acceptance and passing on of values are the goals on which our school's past, present and future are built. Our aim is to run a <strong>student-centred</strong> and, through that, <strong>partner-oriented</strong> school. Our school is <strong>open</strong> to social expectations and <strong>changing labour market needs</strong>, strives to meet these tasks through continuous <strong>innovation and renewal</strong>, and cooperates mutually with its professional partners.</p><p>In our teaching and educational work, we take into account and build into our programme the needs of parents, students and employers. In the modern, well-equipped classrooms, laboratories, IT workshops and industrial modelling workshops located in the school's two buildings, students can acquire the theoretical and practical knowledge of their trades.</p>"}, {"title": "Our famous former students", "html": "<p>Our school has always taken great care to develop its students' abilities as broadly as possible and, alongside its recognised high-standard vocational training, to provide a higher level of general education. Among our former students we are proud to count, among others, the world-famous writer <strong>Nádas Péter</strong>, the philosopher <strong>Vajda Mihály</strong>, one of the founders of the Budapest School, <strong>Kovács László</strong>, former foreign minister and European Union commissioner, as well as outstanding figures of Hungarian classical and popular music such as <strong>Oberfrank Géza</strong>, former conductor of the Opera House, <strong>Demjén Ferenc</strong>, <strong>Korda György</strong> and <strong>Földes László (Hobo)</strong>.</p>"}, {"title": "International relations", "html": "<p>We pay special attention to nurturing international relations and take part continuously in the Erasmus+ programme. We currently have partner schools and partner institutions in Denmark, Portugal, Poland, Croatia, Spain, Greece, Lithuania, Italy and Cyprus.</p>"}, {"title": "Recognition and maintainer", "html": "<p>In the HVG publication “Secondary School 2019”, our school achieved 10th place nationwide in the ranking of vocational secondary schools. According to the publication, “The vocational secondary schools at the top of the ranking belong to the elite of vocational training […]”.</p><p>Our school's maintainer since 1 July 2015 has been the Budapest Technical Vocational Training Centre.</p>"}]} openFirst={true} />
  <VideoEmbed heading={"School history"} url={"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d3YG5QNkXA8"} title={"School history"} />
  <VideoEmbed heading={"Petrik Lajos"} url={"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GHqyCVSEb7M"} title={"Petrik Lajos"} />
  <DataTable heading={"Awards and recognition"} columns={["Date", "Award"]} rows={[{"cells": ["May 2013", "Quality Award for International Cooperation Culture – for the Leonardo project “Let's Play Chemistry!”"]}, {"cells": ["18 May 2018", "Digital Theme Week 2018 – Innovative Teacher Award to project leader Tóth Éva for the Be Digitally Aware project"]}, {"cells": ["8 June 2019", "Digital Theme Week 2019 – teacher competition, 2nd place to project leader Tóth Éva for the project WorkIT"]}, {"cells": ["8 June 2019", "Digital Theme Week 2019 – Oracle Academy Program “Code a STEM project!” special prize for the WorkIt project, in the vocational institution category"]}, {"cells": ["12 March 2020", "#petrikcodeweek institutional special prize in the Code Week competition (DPMK – 2019/10)\nVocational Training Award 2020 – Innovation category, for the project Digital Theme Week at Petrik: WorkIt"]}, {"cells": ["1 July 2020", "Digital Theme Week 2020 – “Quality Award Teacher” special prize to project leader Tóth Éva for the project Socially Re-designed"]}, {"cells": ["2020–1999", "Richter Gedeon Foundation – Award for Hungarian Chemistry Education\n2020 – Dr. Dóbéné Cserjés Edit · 2016 – Vámos István · 2015 – Dr. Stankovics Éva · 2013 – Baranyiné C. Veres Anna · 2005 – Fogarasi József · 2004 – Dr. Lovas Zoltánné · 2003 – Ütő Piroska · 2000 – Kisszékelyi Gyuláné · 1999 – Surányi Istvánné"]}]} />
  <LinkList heading={"Further reading"} items={[{"title": "The history of the school's B building", "href": "https://petrikbepulet.webnode.hu/", "meta": "petrikbepulet.webnode.hu"}]} />
</Layout>
